{"name":"Seaweed Salad","hex":"#7d7b55","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seaweed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous marine algae, such as a kelp.","Any of various fresh water plants and algae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seaweed"},{"term":"salad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food consisting principally of raw vegetables (especially greens, e.g. lettuce), other savoury ingredients (typically cooked), fruit, or confectionary; often involving two or more such ingredients mixed together, with larger items cut or torn into small pieces, and usually with a dressing or binding; usually served cold or at room temperature, as a dish or savoury sandwich filling.","One or more raw vegetables of the kind used in salads; typically greens (especially lettuce)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wakame","blocks":[{"text":"Wakame (Undaria pinnatifida) is a species of kelp native to cold, temperate coasts of the northwest Pacific Ocean. As an edible seaweed, it has a subtly sweet, but distinctive and strong flavour and satiny texture. It is most often served in soups and salads."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/CSIRO_ScienceImage_952_Undaria_pinnatifida_Japanese_kelp.jpg/330px-CSIRO_ScienceImage_952_Undaria_pinnatifida_Japanese_kelp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakame"},{"title":"Seaweed","blocks":[{"text":"Seaweed, or macroalgae, refers to thousands of species of macroscopic, multicellular, marine algae. The term includes some types of Rhodophyta (red), Phaeophyta (brown) and Chlorophyta (green) macroalgae. Seaweed species such as kelps provide essential nursery habitat for fisheries and other marine species and thus protect food sources; other species, such as planktonic algae, play a vital role in capturing carbon and producing at least 50% of Earth's oxygen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fucus_serratus_2015-09-08_ag_M0010140.jpg/330px-Fucus_serratus_2015-09-08_ag_M0010140.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seaweed"},{"title":"Salad","blocks":[{"text":"A salad is a dish consisting of mixed ingredients, frequently vegetables. They are typically served chilled or at room temperature, though some can be served warm. Condiments called salad dressings, which exist in a variety of flavors, are usually used to make a salad."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Salad_platter.jpg/330px-Salad_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salad"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Korea-Miyeok-01.jpg/500px-Korea-Miyeok-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Korea-Miyeok-01.jpg/500px-Korea-Miyeok-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dried miyeok (wakame) at a market in South Korea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKorea-Miyeok-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Boiled_wakame.jpg/330px-Boiled_wakame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Boiled_wakame.jpg/960px-Boiled_wakame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Boiled_wakame.jpg/330px-Boiled_wakame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoiled_wakame.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/